Description: Estimates the mean, the covariance and the score laws of a random
    function when each subject contributes a single noisy observation at a
    random time. The model has two independent, standardized, non-Gaussian
    scores, which identify the covariance from the law of one observation.
    Estimation is by sieve maximum likelihood, with the score laws in
    standardized two-component normal mixtures or in atomic laws on a grid.
    The package also predicts curves from one observation, computes
    identification diagnostics, and generates the data of the simulation
    designs of the accompanying paper.
